ys from Republican-leaning firms. Averages across aggregators put the race near a 10-point Cooper lead.\n\nCooper has also built a large financial edge, raising roughly $35 million and holding over $20 million on hand, while outside groups have spent heavily attacking Whatley. Expert raters overwhelmingly call the race a Likely or Safe Democratic flip, and prediction markets price Cooper's chances at 94 to 96 percent. Whatley has campaigned on tax cuts with Trump's endorsement, but the evidence points to a Democratic pickup.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9425, "margin": 7.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.93, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9375, "margin": 8.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9346, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9278, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9264, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.939, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9386, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9577, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9512, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9379, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9381, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.956, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9414, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9393, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9452, "margin": 9.2}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.965, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.965, "margin": 9.5}]}